## 💾 BumpPointer Allocator

### O(1) Allocation Strategy

```rust
pub struct BumpPointerAllocator {
    heap_start: usize,      // 0x5000
    heap_end: usize,        // 0xFFFE
    current_ptr: usize,     // Next free address
}

impl BumpPointerAllocator {
    pub fn allocate(&mut self, size: u64) -> Result<usize, String> {
        let addr = self.current_ptr;
        let new_ptr = addr + size as usize;

        if new_ptr > self.heap_end {
            return Err("Heap overflow".to_string());
        }

        self.current_ptr = new_ptr;
        Ok(addr)
    }

    pub fn reset(&mut self) {
        self.current_ptr = self.heap_start;
    }
}
```

**优势**:
- O(1) allocation (just increment pointer)
- Zero fragmentation after compaction
- Cache-friendly (linear memory layout)

**缺点**:
- Requires periodic compaction
- Cannot free individual objects (until GC + compaction)

