## 📊 Integration Strategy

### Before & After Compaction

```
Before (Fragmented):
┌─────────┬─────┬──────────┬─────┐
│ Array1  │FREE │ Array2   │Str2 │
│   (5)   │ (3) │   (7)    │ (4) │
│ 0x5000  │     │ 0x5009   │     │
├─────────┼─────┼──────────┼─────┤
Stack: [0x5000, 0x5009, 0x5010]
Free: 3 bytes (wasted)

After (Compacted):
┌─────────┬──────────┬─────┬─────────┐
│ Array1  │ Array2   │Str2 │  FREE   │
│  (5)    │   (7)    │ (4) │  (7)    │
│0x5000   │ 0x5005   │0x500C│0x500F  │
├─────────┼──────────┼─────┼─────────┤
Stack: [0x5000, 0x5005, 0x500C]
Free: 7 bytes (contiguous!)
```

### Compaction Trigger Strategy

```rust
pub fn should_compact(&self) -> bool {
    let free_bytes = self.heap_end - self.heap_ptr;
    let allocated_bytes = self.allocated_bytes();
    let total_heap = self.heap_end - self.heap_start;

    let fragmentation_ratio = free_bytes as f64 / total_heap as f64;
    let allocated_ratio = allocated_bytes as f64 / total_heap as f64;

    // Compact if:
    // 1. Fragmentation > 20%, OR
    // 2. Allocation attempts fail but total space available
    if fragmentation_ratio > 0.20 && allocated_ratio > 0.30 {
        return true;
    }

    false
}
```

